{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-71888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0\\le y<2}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-71888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/f4ee8fbf9a7670a7d0e0b7488bccbf014f8db8fff0154c7db025f2b071aec566.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/9fc733f6966b016c93b6ee6a305c5af5ee4fa432dad5d95e28061fd2a0d33efb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-71888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c83fcbd228dfba91a0ef617a64e3ef6287ce522e60d736a7e00395d18557be8"} {"question" "q-71888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-71888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1"] ["math" "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2"] ["math" "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4"] ["math" "0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2"] ["math" "0\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-71888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/2bb25857047d7a0200d4c58ee3756b0efa0f2d13aaca8664b1fe49414c18a461.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=-x\\,}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c83fcbd228dfba91a0ef617a64e3ef6287ce522e60d736a7e00395d18557be8"} {"question" "q-161596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}<-x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}>-x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}\\ge -x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}\\le -x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/ff1f735266f66879834e02ca7601e90e40dfa7929e5796d4a3f8cb4ff2828de7.png)\n\n  \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c83fcbd228dfba91a0ef617a64e3ef6287ce522e60d736a7e00395d18557be8"} {"question" "q-161601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?  \n\n- $∂A\\cap A\\ne ∅$\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A=\\text{int}\\,A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/2273cd843c4bfaeaff10d49d3400d7661262673639a66034638d805eef5b1e47.png)\n\n   \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/5e473584ef5193b434ff6c138b08c4fbd9111a37252019143b1afb2d48c913c6.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have  $∂A\\cap A=∅.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c83fcbd228dfba91a0ef617a64e3ef6287ce522e60d736a7e00395d18557be8"} {"question" "q-161652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I  only"] ["text" "I and III  only"] ["text" "II  only"] ["text" "II and III  only"] ["text" "III  only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III  only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/c0b805c707981b9b6fcfa2ed387ad32a024fc845e6fd355a4b751ede4ad6a97e.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/assets/69708aa698c38f8a29d3eb69083f893fd8fca183bd713387456624fc38b86fe9.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c83fcbd228dfba91a0ef617a64e3ef6287ce522e60d736a7e00395d18557be8"} {"question" "q-161721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2"] ["math" "0<x<2,\\text{ }0\\le y\\le 2"] ["math" "0\\le x<2,\\text{ }0\\le y<2"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 2,\\text{ }0<y<2"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 2,\\text{ }0\\le y\\le 2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"} {"question" "q-161721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072304/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d7e5f8f05d20c1b7cd8bf799d6977d8a465ab912b5e038780f0dbc16fb59357"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2658 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
